The engines use only the standard library of their language. No third-party
code is included in this repository.

The runner (runner/) is built with third-party Rust crates, fetched at build
time and not included in this repository. Its direct dependencies, each
pinned to one version in runner/Cargo.toml and runner/Cargo.lock:

  zenoh 1.9.0         EPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/eclipse-zenoh/zenoh
  serde 1.0.228       MIT OR Apache-2.0      https://github.com/serde-rs/serde
  serde_norway 0.9.42 MIT OR Apache-2.0      https://github.com/cafkafk/serde-yaml
  rustls 0.23.46      Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT  https://github.com/rustls/rustls
  rustls-pki-types 1.16.0  MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/rustls/pki-types
  x509-parser 0.18.1  MIT OR Apache-2.0      https://github.com/rusticata/x509-parser
  ring 0.17.14        Apache-2.0 AND ISC     https://github.com/briansmith/ring
  webpki-roots 1.0.12 CDLA-Permissive-2.0    https://github.com/rustls/webpki-roots

Every crate those depend on, with its version and license, is listed in
runner/THIRD-PARTY.md. The .deb package carries this file and LICENSE in
/usr/share/doc/goat-processors/. The packs and vectors are original work;
coordinates in the vectors are notional points in open ocean.

Recorded ship trajectories (tools/bench/data/recorded-ships.json) are derived
from "Vessel Traffic (AIS)" published by the NOAA Office for Coastal
Management and the Bureau of Ocean Energy Management on MarineCadastre.gov
(daily file AIS_2023_01_01; https://marinecadastre.gov/ais). That material is
a work of the U.S. Government and is not subject to copyright protection
within the United States (17 U.S.C. 403 notice). Only times and positions
were kept; vessel identifiers were removed and positions were moved to a
notional point in open ocean (tools/bench/recorded.py).
